    "//#typecheck:scripts": {
      "description": "Root-level task: tsc --noEmit over the repo-level tooling in scripts/. Prefix //# ensures repo-root-only. Exists because NOTHING typechecked this tree: the package-scoped typecheck task cannot reach scripts/ (it belongs to no workspace package), and //#lint:scripts is TYPE-AWARE but reports lint rules only -- it builds a TS program and then never surfaces the general TS diagnostic set, so a noUncheckedIndexedAccess violation passed lint while silently returning undefined at runtime. That exact hole produced a FALSE MERGE: an unclassifiable check was dropped from every bucket, the rollup reported green, and a genuinely failed check would have been merged. ci.yml already recognises this shape and solves it for e2e/ with a dedicated tsc step (E2E Typecheck); scripts/ is the identical shape and had no equivalent. Completes the root-tooling triad with //#lint:scripts and //#test:scripts. Runs the committed root script typecheck:scripts verbatim -- it is NOT a second compiler invocation. WIRED INTO __ci_fast__ (2026-08-08). It was deliberately ungated at registration: the first run reported 89 pre-existing errors (58 after the scripts/tsconfig.json fix), and gating on that immediately would have made every branch in a ~50-worktree estate unmergeable at once and taught the team to ignore the tool -- the same adoption reasoning //#knip documents. scripts/typecheck-scripts-ratchet.guard.test.ts held the line meanwhile (errors may fall, never rise) and named this promotion as its own exit condition. The count reached 0 by fixing every error at its root -- no ceiling raised, no compiler flag disabled, no suppression pragma -- so the ratchet is deleted and the gate is live. ci-fast-covers-typecheck-scripts.guard.test.ts now asserts this wiring, so a future edit that drops it fails a test instead of silently reopening the hole. cache:false -- a pass/fail check with no cacheable output, matching lint:scripts and test:scripts. Run: pnpm exec turbo run typecheck:scripts.",
