    "//#lint:e2e": {
      "description": "Root-level task: ESLint the Playwright acceptance suite in e2e/. Prefix //# ensures repo-root-only. EXISTS BECAUSE NOTHING LINTED THIS TREE. @fleet/e2e is a workspace member but declares only a typecheck script, so turbo run lint --filter=@fleet/e2e ran its DEPENDENCY and reported success without linting a single spec; ci.yml has a dedicated E2E Typecheck step for exactly this reason (the specs sit at the repo root, outside any package tsconfig) but had no lint equivalent. Meanwhile eslint.config.mjs carefully binds e2e/**/*.ts to e2e/tsconfig.json for type-aware rules -- configuration that was never executed. This is the THIRD instance of the same hole in this repo, after //#lint:scripts and //#typecheck:scripts: a check that exists in principle and nowhere in practice. Turborepo documents the root-scoped //# task as the answer for a tree that belongs to no package, since its conventions assume apps/ and packages/ and anything outside them is simply never visited. Wired into __ci_fast__ so an e2e lint violation fails the PR gate; the immediate motivation is the budget-SSOT rule (no-restricted-syntax on *_BUDGET_MS declarations), which would otherwise be inert config. cache:false -- a pass/fail check with no cacheable output, matching lint:scripts. dependsOn ^build for the SAME reason lint and typecheck document: e2e/helpers/wait-for-projection.ts imports DispatchBoardResponseSchema from @fleet/sync-protocol, and the type-aware no-unsafe-* rules resolve that through the package EMITTED .d.ts, not its source. Without ^build a clean checkout has no dist/, the import resolves to any, and the rules fire -- observed 2026-08-20 as five no-unsafe-* errors on an unchanged file, immediately after a sync-protocol source edit staled the build. It had only ever passed by relying on a warm dist/ from an earlier run, the identical trap the typecheck description records. Run: pnpm exec turbo run lint:e2e.",
