    "//#format:check": {
      "description": "Root-level task: assert every file matches the committed Prettier style. Prefix //# ensures repo-root-only: .prettierrc governs the whole tree and belongs to no workspace package. ROOT CAUSE THIS CLOSES: the repo carried .prettierrc, .prettierignore and the prettier devDependency, AND eslint-config-prettier -- which exists precisely to TURN OFF every ESLint formatting rule so Prettier can own them. So ESLint was told to stop enforcing style, and Prettier was never run: no format script, no hook, no CI step. //#knip reported prettier as an unused devDependency and was right in the only sense that matters -- nothing invoked it. Formatting was enforced by NEITHER tool while two config files described it in detail, which is the decorative-control shape this repo has now closed seven times. 2026 guidance is explicit that ESLint and Prettier run as SEPARATE tools with eslint-config-prettier as the bridge; the bridge was built and the far side was missing. cache:false -- a pass/fail check over working-tree state, matching lint:scripts and test:scripts. Run: pnpm exec turbo run format:check.",
