    "//#bump:turbo": {
      "description": "Root-level task: bump the turbo devDependency version for the whole repo. Unlike bump:pnpm (which drives the corepack packageManager pin), turbo is an ordinary devDependency, so the correct bump is a spec rewrite in package.json plus a lockfile update -- not corepack use. The pure decision core (scripts/bump-turbo.ts planTurboBump) preserves the range operator (^, ~, or exact) and refuses a non-semver target; the thin driver refuses on a dirty tree so the bump is always an isolated, reviewable commit, then runs pnpm install --lockfile-only. Replaces the uncaptured hand-edit + bare pnpm install idiom that drifted (wrong range, forgotten lockfile, no runtime verification). Prefix //# ensures repo-root-only. cache:false (side-effecting, network-resolving). Run: pnpm exec turbo run bump:turbo -- <version>.",
      "cache": false
